PROMPT 1 — MongoDB Atlas cluster + connection setup
I have a Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript) project called Baithak-School-Website. I need to connect it to MongoDB Atlas (cloud). Do the following:

Install the required package: npm install mongodb
Create the file lib/mongodb.ts with a singleton MongoClient connection using the MONGODB_URI environment variable. Use this exact pattern so the connection is reused across hot reloads in dev:
Export a clientPromise (Promise<MongoClient>)
In development, cache it on the global object to survive HMR reloads
In production, create a new client each time
Add MONGODB_URI to .env.local (I will fill in the value): MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/baithak?retryWrites=true&w=majority
Add .env.local to .gitignore if not already there.
The database name is: baithak Collections will be: news_stories, donations Do not create any API routes yet. Just the connection file.
